      "title": "Amazon to invest $7 billion in India's renewable energy projects by 2030",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/amazon-to-invest-7-billion-in-india-s-renewable-energy-projects-by-2030-126111700633_1.html",
      "description": "Amazon on Tuesday announced plans to invest USD 7 billion (about Rs 65,393 crore) in renewable energy projects in India by 2030, in addition to the USD 4 billion already contracted, as it unveiled four new wind and solar projects with a combined capacity of 934 megawatts.\nThe company said the investment makes it one of India's leading corporate purchasers of carbon-free energy.\nThe four initiatives consist of a 234 MW wind farm in Karnataka -- marking Amazon's largest contracted wind project in Asia to date -- alongside a 200 MW hybrid solar-and-wind facility in the same state, a 300 MW solar installation in Madhya Pradesh, and a 200 MW solar project in Rajasthan.\nSecured through power purchase agreements (PPAs), the projects are part of the USD 4 billion in renewable energy projects already contracted by Amazon in India, the company said.\nOnce operational, Amazon's renewable energy portfolio in the country will have a combined capacity of more than 2 gigawatts (GW), enough to ...",
